From 0ed6c352f4afb54a0a6794abaa11ae80266004f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Che Haijun <chehaijun@Mac.localdomain>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:50:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(research): reading notes and a methods record

Two phases of a qualitative study had no support at all: familiarisation and
write-up. Both are now covered, which closes four of the six phases of a thematic
analysis.

Reading notes (schema v3). A document gains a memo, shown as a strip under the
reader header and saved as you type. The familiarisation phase produces exactly
this kind of note, and previously there was nowhere to put it. migrate() upgrades
v1 and v2 projects stepwise, so existing codebooks, codings and offsets are
untouched.

Methods record. methods_narrative() assembles a Markdown account of how the
analysis was actually carried out, read from the project state and the audit
trail: the data, coding totals, how the codebook changed over time, the theme
tree with definitions and anchor examples, how much AI assistance was used and
what was done with it, and the integrity guarantees. Exported as a fourth format.

The point is not the export itself. Reconstructing a methods section from memory
two weeks after finishing the analysis is a real cost, and no existing tool
removes it. This does, because the process is already recorded.
